WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:04.068
Start from any application page Move to the Admin

00:00:04.068 --> 00:00:06.906
menu in the top navigation and click it In

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.370
the menu that opens click Portfolios This is the

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.445
place to create and organize regular brokerage accounts decide

00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:17.857
which accounts belong to Owner and create regular aggregate

00:00:17.857 --> 00:00:18.378
views

00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:24.869
On Manage Portfolios click New Portfolio A regular portfolio

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:27.590
is the real account record It owns its own

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:33.632
holdings cash snapshot transaction history and imports Create one

00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:37.043
regular portfolio for each brokerage account you want to

00:00:37.043 --> 00:00:38.111
track separately

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.327
Type a clear account name in the New Portfolio

00:00:42.327 --> 00:00:46.442
dialog then click OK In this walkthrough the two

00:00:46.455 --> 00:00:51.233
import targets are Fidelity Income Demo and Fidelity Activity

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:55.127
Demo I also create a small Fidelity Creation Walkthrough

00:00:55.127 --> 00:00:57.262
account on screen so you can see the real

00:00:57.275 --> 00:00:59.202
creation process end to end

00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:04.595
After creation set the Broker Source to Fidelity The

00:01:04.595 --> 00:01:08.046
two demo accounts are user-owned and their Owner checkboxes

00:01:08.059 --> 00:01:11.887
are selected Owner is an optional personal rollup it

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.533
combines only the regular user-owned accounts you check It

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:18.306
is not a brokerage account so you never import

00:01:18.319 --> 00:01:20.793
a Fidelity file into Owner itself

00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:26.872
Select Fidelity Income Demo in the portfolio selector Then

00:01:26.885 --> 00:01:31.052
open Admin Import Broker Import and Step 1 Positions

00:01:31.482 --> 00:01:38.630
Choose Fidelity and upload fidelity_positions_Demo . xlsx The positions

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.640
file establishes the account’s current holdings and cash so

00:01:42.653 --> 00:01:44.528
this is normally the first import

00:01:46.224 --> 00:01:50.612
Use Preview before importing The live preview identifies Fidelity

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:54.479
Income Demo as both the file account and destination

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:58.841
It shows eight VTI shares one hundred fifty JEPQ

00:01:58.841 --> 00:02:02.474
shares and the separate cash row After verifying that

00:02:02.474 --> 00:02:07.071
result click Import into Fidelity Income Demo The import

00:02:07.071 --> 00:02:09.974
was performed in the test account and refreshed its

00:02:09.987 --> 00:02:10.964
two positions

00:02:12.644 --> 00:02:17.214
Now select Fidelity Activity Demo In Broker Import click

00:02:17.214 --> 00:02:24.233
Step 2 Transactions and upload fidelity_transactions_Demo . xlsx The

00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:28.191
preview finds two buys one dividend and one DRIP

00:02:28.204 --> 00:02:31.785
reinvestment I performed this import in the test account

00:02:32.214 --> 00:02:35.431
Because it already has a broker positions snapshot the

00:02:35.431 --> 00:02:39.142
transaction import records the history while keeping the current

00:02:39.142 --> 00:02:40.300
broker share counts

00:02:42.024 --> 00:02:44.081
To inspect a test account choose it in the

00:02:44.094 --> 00:02:49.876
top portfolio selector and open Portfolio Holdings Fidelity Income

00:02:49.889 --> 00:02:54.954
Demo now shows its imported positions eight VTI shares

00:02:55.201 --> 00:02:58.665
and one hundred fifty JEPQ shares Those are this

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:03.118
regular account’s own positions they remain separate even when

00:03:03.118 --> 00:03:04.160
included in Owner

00:03:05.841 --> 00:03:09.474
Switch the same selector to Fidelity Activity Demo then

00:03:09.474 --> 00:03:14.435
stay on Portfolio Holdings Its imported history supports twelve

00:03:14.448 --> 00:03:19.122
VTI shares and point three seven JEPI shares Notice

00:03:19.122 --> 00:03:22.755
that VTI is shared by both test accounts while

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.659
JEPI exists only in this activity account

00:03:27.354 --> 00:03:30.674
Now choose Owner in the portfolio selector and open

00:03:30.674 --> 00:03:35.128
Holdings Owner combines matching tickers from its selected member

00:03:35.128 --> 00:03:39.125
accounts into one row Here the Owner VTI row

00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:43.826
shows twenty shares eight from Fidelity Income Demo plus

00:03:43.826 --> 00:03:47.693
twelve from Fidelity Activity Demo This proves that matching

00:03:47.706 --> 00:03:50.818
ticker shares aggregate together in Owner

00:03:52.504 --> 00:03:55.538
The unique tickers illustrate the other half of the

00:03:55.538 --> 00:04:00.512
rule JEPQ appears only in Fidelity Income Demo so

00:04:00.525 --> 00:04:03.715
Owner shows the same one hundred fifty shares JEPI

00:04:03.715 --> 00:04:07.660
appears only in Fidelity Activity Demo so Owner shows

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.629
the same point three seven shares Owner is a

00:04:10.642 --> 00:04:14.535
combined view not a data move Regular aggregates work

00:04:14.548 --> 00:04:19.132
the same way create as many named read-only groupings

00:04:19.145 --> 00:04:21.905
as needed without changing the real account data
